---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import CompareNotesCallout from '../../components/CompareNotesCallout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Intelligence for marketing"
  description="How marketing teams turn disconnected evidence into connected understanding, stronger narratives and knowledge that compounds."
  pageType="collection"
>
  <article class="container-site py-20">
    <div class="marketing-inner">
      <header class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-6">Flagship application</p>
        <h1 class="t-display mb-6">Editorial Intelligence for marketing</h1>
        <p class="marketing-lead mb-8">Marketing has become more specialised. It has not necessarily become more connected.</p>
        <div class="prose-section mb-8">
          <p>Research teams uncover customer insight. Product marketers define positioning. Content teams create articles, video and campaigns. Performance marketers optimise channels. Customer marketers capture stories. Sales teams hear objections. AI can now generate content from almost all of it.</p>
          <p>On paper, marketing has never had access to more knowledge. Yet many organisations still struggle to develop distinctive narratives, consistent positioning and campaigns that improve over time.</p>
          <p>The problem is rarely a lack of activity. Valuable knowledge remains trapped inside specialist functions.</p>
          <p>Editorial Intelligence helps those functions work from a stronger shared understanding.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="marketing-actions">
          <a href="/work/narrative-audit" class="marketing-btn">Explore the Narrative Audit</a>
          <a href="/applications" class="marketing-link">See all applications →</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">The hidden cost</p>
        <h2 class="marketing-h2 mb-8">Every team learns. The organisation does not always learn with them.</h2>
        <div class="prose-section">
          <p>Specialisation is one of modern marketing's greatest strengths. It is also one of its least discussed challenges.</p>
          <p>As functions become more expert, they naturally become more focused on their own objectives. Research improves research. Campaigns improve campaigns. Customer stories improve customer marketing.</p>
          <p>But effectiveness inside individual functions does not automatically create understanding across the organisation.</p>
          <p>Research may never influence product messaging. Campaign learning may never reshape thought leadership. Sales conversations may never reach the people planning the next campaign. Customer stories may remain isolated examples rather than revealing broader patterns.</p>
          <p>None of this happens because people are doing poor work. It happens because organisations have become better at producing knowledge than connecting it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="marketing-principle mt-10">
          <p class="t-label mb-3">The problem is not information</p>
          <p>It is movement. Valuable knowledge arrives, gets used, is stored and then stops shaping future work.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">The connective capability</p>
        <h2 class="marketing-h2 mb-8">Editorial Intelligence sits between organisational evidence and marketing execution.</h2>
        <p class="marketing-intro mb-10">It is not another channel or specialist team. It is the capability that helps evidence move between them.</p>

        <div class="marketing-stack" aria-label="Editorial Intelligence marketing stack">
          <div class="stack-layer">
            <p class="stack-label">Marketing execution</p>
            <div class="stack-grid">
              <span>Campaign strategy</span>
              <span>Thought leadership</span>
              <span>Product marketing</span>
              <span>Content marketing</span>
              <span>Customer marketing</span>
              <span>Sales enablement</span>
              <span>Executive communications</span>
              <span>AI visibility</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="stack-core">
            <p class="stack-core-title">Editorial Intelligence</p>
            <p>Capture · Connect · Interpret · Frame · Activate · Learn</p>
          </div>

          <div class="stack-layer">
            <p class="stack-label">Organisational evidence</p>
            <div class="stack-grid">
              <span>Research</span>
              <span>Customer insight</span>
              <span>Product knowledge</span>
              <span>Sales conversations</span>
              <span>Campaign response</span>
              <span>Search behaviour</span>
              <span>Market signals</span>
              <span>Executive expertise</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">Across the function</p>
        <h2 class="marketing-h2 mb-10">What Editorial Intelligence contributes</h2>
        <div class="capability-grid">
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">01</span>
            <h3>Campaign strategy</h3>
            <p>Finds the strongest evidence-backed tension before the team begins producing assets.</p>
            <small>Creates: narrative hypotheses, evidence maps, campaign direction.</small>
          </article>
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">02</span>
            <h3>Product marketing</h3>
            <p>Connects product capability, customer language and market evidence into a clearer position.</p>
            <small>Creates: customer tensions, message architecture, proof themes.</small>
          </article>
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">03</span>
            <h3>Content and editorial</h3>
            <p>Turns isolated production into connected narratives and reusable organisational knowledge.</p>
            <small>Creates: editorial systems, throughlines, knowledge that compounds.</small>
          </article>
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">04</span>
            <h3>Thought leadership</h3>
            <p>Recognises original positions across research, practitioner experience and customer evidence.</p>
            <small>Creates: distinctive arguments, evidence-backed points of view.</small>
          </article>
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">05</span>
            <h3>Customer marketing</h3>
            <p>Extracts recurring patterns from customer evidence rather than treating every story as an isolated success.</p>
            <small>Creates: transformation patterns, customer language, reusable proof.</small>
          </article>
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">06</span>
            <h3>Performance marketing</h3>
            <p>Interprets campaign response as evidence that can improve positioning and future decisions.</p>
            <a href="/applications/performance-marketing">Explore the specialist application →</a>
          </article>
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">07</span>
            <h3>Sales enablement</h3>
            <p>Carries customer language, objections and proof into material that supports commercial conversations.</p>
            <small>Creates: objection maps, proof libraries, message feedback loops.</small>
          </article>
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">08</span>
            <h3>Executive communications</h3>
            <p>Turns experience and expertise into credible positions that can be reused across channels.</p>
            <small>Creates: narrative platforms, speaking themes, executive points of view.</small>
          </article>
          <article class="capability-card">
            <span class="capability-num">09</span>
            <h3>AI visibility</h3>
            <p>Makes organisational expertise more coherent, explicit and retrievable across search and AI systems.</p>
            <a href="/work/ai-visibility-audit">Explore the AI Visibility Audit →</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">The learning loop</p>
        <h2 class="marketing-h2 mb-8">Marketing becomes a learning system rather than a production system.</h2>
        <div class="learning-loop" aria-label="Editorial Intelligence marketing learning loop">
          <div class="loop-step"><span>01</span><strong>Evidence</strong><p>Research, customers, sales, products and market signals.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-arrow">↓</div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>02</span><strong>Narrative</strong><p>Patterns become arguments, positions and hypotheses.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-arrow">↓</div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>03</span><strong>Activation</strong><p>Campaigns, content, sales material and communications.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-arrow">↓</div>
          <div class="loop-step"><span>04</span><strong>Audience response</strong><p>Behaviour, questions, objections, engagement and outcomes.</p></div>
          <div class="loop-arrow">↓</div>
          <div class="loop-step loop-step--accent"><span>05</span><strong>Editorial synthesis</strong><p>Learning is interpreted and returned to the evidence base.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-section mt-10">
          <p>Every campaign should leave the organisation knowing something it did not know before.</p>
          <p>That understanding then improves the next campaign. Marketing begins to compound because its knowledge compounds.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">Clear boundaries</p>
        <h2 class="marketing-h2 mb-8">What Editorial Intelligence does not replace</h2>
        <div class="boundary-grid">
          <div class="boundary-card">
            <p class="t-label mb-4">Specialist marketing owns</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Brand strategy</li>
              <li>Media strategy and buying</li>
              <li>Marketing operations and CRM</li>
              <li>SEO and channel expertise</li>
              <li>Product marketing practice</li>
              <li>Creative and communications delivery</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="boundary-card boundary-card--accent">
            <p class="t-label mb-4">Editorial Intelligence connects</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Evidence across specialist functions</li>
              <li>Narrative and strategic framing</li>
              <li>Customer language and market signals</li>
              <li>Learning across campaigns and projects</li>
              <li>Organisational memory</li>
              <li>Knowledge that compounds</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">Why now</p>
        <h2 class="marketing-h2 mb-8">AI makes production cheaper. It makes judgement more valuable.</h2>
        <div class="prose-section">
          <p>Creating another article, image or campaign variation is no longer the difficult part.</p>
          <p>The constraint is moving towards judgement: which customer problem deserves attention, which evidence is strongest, which campaign result matters beyond the dashboard and which idea should become the organisation's position.</p>
          <p>AI can increase output without increasing understanding. Editorial Intelligence helps organisations decide what deserves to be produced, why it matters and what should be learned from the response.</p>
          <p class="font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)]">As content becomes cheaper, connected understanding becomes more valuable.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">Connected proof</p>
        <h2 class="marketing-h2 mb-10">See the system in practice</h2>
        <div class="related-grid">
          <a href="/narratives/hidden-hours" class="related-card"><span>Research to narrative</span><strong>Hidden Hours</strong><p>How evidence became an organising idea across content, events and campaign activation.</p></a>
          <a href="/frameworks/editorial-activation" class="related-card"><span>Framework</span><strong>Editorial Activation</strong><p>How an idea moves across channels and returns new evidence to the system.</p></a>
          <a href="/applications/performance-marketing" class="related-card"><span>Specialist application</span><strong>Performance marketing</strong><p>How behavioural response can strengthen wider organisational understanding.</p></a>
          <a href="/work/ai-visibility-audit" class="related-card"><span>Diagnostic</span><strong>AI Visibility Audit</strong><p>How organisational knowledge becomes visible, coherent and retrievable.</p></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-8">
        <p class="t-label mb-4">Start with what you already know</p>
        <h2 class="marketing-h2 mb-6">The strongest marketing argument may already exist inside your organisation.</h2>
        <div class="prose-section mb-8">
          <p>A Narrative Audit reviews existing research, customer insight, campaign material and organisational expertise to identify the argument already present, the evidence supporting it and the gaps worth exploring next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="marketing-actions mb-10">
          <a href="/work/narrative-audit" class="marketing-btn">Explore the Narrative Audit</a>
          <a href="/compare-notes" class="marketing-link">Compare notes →</a>
        </div>
        <CompareNotesCallout
          body="I’m testing how Editorial Intelligence can help marketing teams connect research, customer evidence, campaign learning and internal expertise."
          linkLabel="Spend 30 minutes comparing approaches"
        />
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .marketing-inner { max-width: 48rem; }
  .marketing-lead { font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.65rem); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); }
  .marketing-h2 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.45rem); line-height: 1.2; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .marketing-intro { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); }
  .prose-section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .prose-section p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); }
  .marketing-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .marketing-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem; background: var(--color-ink); color: var(--color-surface); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .marketing-link { color: var(--color-ink-secondary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .marketing-btn:hover, .marketing-link:hover, .capability-card a:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .marketing-principle { border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; background: var(--color-surface-secondary); }
  .marketing-principle p:last-child { color: var(--color-ink); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .marketing-stack { border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); background: var(--color-surface-secondary); }
  .stack-layer { padding: 1.5rem; }
  .stack-label { font-family: var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 0.68rem; color: var(--color-ink-tertiary); margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .stack-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.65rem; }
  .stack-grid span { padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); color: var(--color-ink-secondary); font-size: 0.84rem; background: var(--color-surface); }
  .stack-core { padding: 1.5rem; text-align: center; border-block: 1px solid var(--color-accent); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 8%, var(--color-surface)); }
  .stack-core-title { color: var(--color-ink); font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .stack-core p:last-child { color: var(--color-ink-secondary); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; }
  .capability-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .capability-card { border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding: 1.4rem; background: var(--color-surface-secondary); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.65rem; }
  .capability-card h3 { color: var(--color-ink); font-size: 1rem; }
  .capability-card p { color: var(--color-ink-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .capability-card small { color: var(--color-ink-tertiary); line-height: 1.55; }
  .capability-card a { color: var(--color-ink); font-size: 0.82rem; text-decoration: none; margin-top: auto; }
  .capability-num { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--color-accent); font-size: 0.68rem; }
  .learning-loop { border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding: 1rem; background: var(--color-surface-secondary); }
  .loop-step { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 9rem 1fr; align-items: start; gap: 0.75rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .loop-step span { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--color-accent); font-size: 0.68rem; }
  .loop-step strong { color: var(--color-ink); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .loop-step p { color: var(--color-ink-secondary); font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .loop-step--accent { border-color: var(--color-accent); }
  .loop-arrow { text-align: center; color: var(--color-accent); padding: 0.3rem; }
  .boundary-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .boundary-card { border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--color-surface-secondary); }
  .boundary-card--accent { border-color: var(--color-accent); }
  .boundary-card ul { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  .related-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .related-card { border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); padding: 1.4rem; text-decoration: none; background: var(--color-surface-secondary); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem; }
  .related-card span { font-family: var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-size: 0.64rem; color: var(--color-accent); }
  .related-card strong { color: var(--color-ink); }
  .related-card p { color: var(--color-ink-secondary); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .related-card:hover { border-color: var(--color-accent); }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .capability-grid, .boundary-grid, .related-grid, .stack-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .loop-step { grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; }
    .loop-step p { grid-column: 2; }
  }
</style>
